  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Traditional music of the Bodo (Boro) of lower Assam accompanies the kherai worship of the Bathou religion, in which the deodhani medium dances, and dances such as the bagurumba of the Bwisagu spring festival. The core ensemble is the long sifung bamboo flute, the kham drum, the bowed serja and jotha cymbals; the flute card stands in for the sifung, the generic drum for the kham and the sarinda card for the serja.",
